    "classification": "normal",
    "type": "social",
    "difficulty": 12,
    "notes": "<h3>Normal | Social</h3>\n<p><em>An ambitious and ostentatiously dressed socialite.</em><br><strong>Motives &amp; Tactics:</strong> Discredit, gain favor, maneuver, scheme</p>\n<p><strong>Difficulty:</strong> 12 | <strong>Thresholds:</strong> 4/8 | <strong>HP:</strong> 3 | <strong>Stress:</strong> 4</p>\n<p><strong>ATK:</strong> -4 | Weapon: Melee | 1d4+2 physical</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Experience:</strong> Socialite +3, Schemer +2</p>\n<h4>Features</h4>\n<p><strong>Scapegoat - Action</strong>: Spend a Fear and target a PC. The Courtier convinces a crowd or prominent individual that the target is the cause of their current conflict or misfortune.</p>\n<p><strong>Devastating Retort - Passive</strong>: A PC who rolls less than 15 on an action roll targeting the Courtier must <strong>mark a Stress</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Bend Ears - Action</strong>: <strong>Mark a Stress</strong> to influence an NPC. That target’s opinion on a matter shifts towards the Courtier&#39;&#39;s preference unless directly opposed to their motives.</p>\n",
